# =============================================================================
# What is tracked, and why
# =============================================================================
#   src/       source code                       -> tracked
#   config/    job/operation parameters          -> tracked
#   docs/      documentation                     -> tracked
#   artifacts/ EVERYTHING generated              -> ignored (this file)
#
# Rule of thumb: if a file is produced by running the toolkit it belongs under
# artifacts/ and is ignored. If a human wrote it and someone else would need it,
# it belongs under src/, config/ or docs/ and is tracked.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated output: logs, session evidence, sensor samples.
# This is the bulk of the tree and pure noise for anyone cloning - the session
# directories alone reached 453 MB on the machine this was organised on.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
artifacts/
# Legacy output locations, kept ignored so an older checkout does not suddenly
# start staging hundreds of megabytes of logs.
runs/
watchdog_sessions/
task_logs/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Personal data: photos of BIOS pages. They document one specific board's
# settings and are of no use to another user, so they are not published. The
# findings that matter are written up in docs/ and in the result documents under
# artifacts/runs/.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
bios_photo/
*.bmp

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Machine-specific configuration. Tool locations differ per machine; keeping them
# out of the repository is what lets it be cloned and used anywhere.
#
# Put your own values in ONE of:
#   %APPDATA%\overclock-toolkit\paths.json     (recommended; outside the repo)
#   config/paths.local.json                    (checkout-local override)
#
# See docs/CONFIGURATION.md for the key names.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
config/paths.local.json
config/paths.json
# Written at trigger time by the non-elevated side before `schtasks /run`.
config/co_task_op.json

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Compiled helpers. memprobe.exe is built from src/bench/memprobe.c by whoever
# needs it; shipping a binary would tie the repository to one compiler and one
# machine.
#   gcc -O2 -o artifacts/build/memprobe.exe src/bench/memprobe.c
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.exe
*.dll
*.obj
*.o
*.pdb

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime state written while a run is in progress.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / OS noise
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.commandcode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local notes. AGENT.md is tracked on purpose (it is the collaboration protocol);
# a personal scratch file is not.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
notes.local.md
*.local.json
*.local.md
